w: Sing, O sing, this bless- ed morn, Un- to us a Child is born,
w: Je- sus Christ, the King of kings, Ma- ker of all world- ly things,
w: God of God, and Light of Light, Comes with mer- cies in- fi- nite;
w: God with us, Em- man- u- el, Deigns for ev- er now to dwell;
w: Truth and Mer- cy show their face, And with lov- ing kiss em- brace;
w: God comes down that man may rise, Lif- ted far a- bove the skies
w: Now we rise, from pri- son free; On we march to vic- to- ry,
w: O re- new us, Lord, we pray, With Thy Spi- rit day by day;
